    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="1282" n="1124" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1124"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        Thompson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 74.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a copy of a dispatch
                    from the consul at Tampico<anchor n="a" xml:id="d231-f1"/> inclosing a newspaper
                    clipping in which it is stated that <pb facs="1283" n="1125" xml:id="pg1125"/>
                    there is an organization among Mexican workmen, especially in the northern part
                    of Mexico, whose purpose is to cause the expulsion of foreign workmen from that
                    country, and that the 16th of September next is set as the time when the
                    expulsion is to begin.</p>
                <p>You will bring the matter to the attention of the Mexican Government and suggest
                    that preventive measures be taken to protect the rights of American citizens, as
                    persons and property may be endangered by the alleged combination.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
